{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And this, the one stricken in the temples [?], behold it is written: 'The beginning of the word of YHWH with Hosea, and YHWH said' — and behold HaShem's mouth did not rebel, far be it, far be it. Rather, Hosea son of Beeri is not Hosea son of Elah, just as the name Enoch is a comprehensive name for four men in the Torah, and Saul of Rehoboth on the River and Saul son of the Canaanite woman and Saul son of Kish, and many likewise. And the beginning of this prophet's prophecy was concerning the kingdom of Jeroboam son of Joash king of Israel, forty years before the exile of Samaria, if his prophecy was at the end of Jeroboam's days, for his son Zechariah reigned after him only six months, and the kingdom of the house of Jehu, which was the kings of Israel, ceased." "And another interpreted: כי לך קח לך — it is speech like the sense of 'goodly portion.'" "And he interpreted: ותהר — like תהרו חשש תלדו קש (you conceive chaff, you give birth to stubble)." "And he said: כי גומר — finished in whoredom." "ובת דבלים — an allusion to Judah and Israel." "And another said: קח לך אשת זנונים — for if you come to take a fitting wife, you will not find one, for behold זנה תזנה הארץ — all the people of the land go whoring after HaShem. And another interpreted:" "קח לך אשת זנונים וילדי זנונים — for behold, similarly, the inhabitants of the land whore from after YHWH, and דיו לעבד להיות כרבו (it is enough for the servant to be like his master)." "Says Abraham the author: Far be it, far be it that HaShem would command to take a wife of harlotry and to beget children of harlotry. And the one who says דיו לעבד להיות כרבו did not say it concerning this, for harlotry from after HaShem is by way of parable, but in a person it is in deed. And the correct in my eyes is that this prophet saw in prophetic visions in a dream of the night that HaShem said to him: Go, take yourself a wife of harlotry, and he went and took a certain woman and she conceived and gave birth — all this in prophetic visions, as he interpreted: 'if he be your prophet, apart from Moses alone — in a vision I make myself known to him; in a dream I speak with him.' And do not wonder how he sees in a dream and goes and takes — for in a dream, a man even without prophecy, and the cows eat them [Genesis 41]. And likewise concerning Isaiah the prophet: 'so my servant Isaiah walked naked and barefoot' — this was in a prophetic vision, for why would the prophet go naked for the sake of Cush and Egypt?! And likewise קח לך לבנה and שכב על צדך השמאלי and ואתה קח לך חטין. Also the matter of the elder and witness to all this that Ezekiel said at the beginning of his book: ואראה מראות אלהים, and he says: במראות אלהים הביאני אל ארץ ישראל. And do not wonder because he did not mention visions at the beginning of the prophecy, for behold it is written: 'the word of YHWH that was to Zechariah,' and there it is written after it: ראיתי הלילה ואשא עיני ואראה. And behold it is written of Abraham במחזה, and so was all his prophecy. And behold He said to him in the way of prophecy: why a wife of harlotry — for זנה תזנה הארץ."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's heading וזה המוכה בסנוירים ('and this, the one stricken in the temples') is obscure; I translate hyper-literally without resolving its meaning.", 7 "The phrase ודבר הזקן והעד ('also the matter of the elder and witness') is elliptical; I translate hyper-literally. The cross-references embedded mid-sentence are left untranslated exactly as Ibn Ezra cites them."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:56.317914122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}